      "section": "3.3 Network",
      "family": "network-ranking",
      "purpose": "Weight influence by time direction and genre crossing, then score nodes with a patched eigenvector centrality",
      "base_or_modification": "modification",
      "summary": "Each musician is a node. An edge from junior to predecessor is up-weighted because that direction is rare, and a cross-genre edge is up-weighted because styles rarely overlap. Weights combine the two with an exponential of the normalized time gap. Importance starts as weighted out-degree and is then iterated with a PageRank-style mix of neighbor score and own score. The result is scaled by its maximum. The distribution fits a power law with R-squared 0.9931.",
      "algorithm": {
        "status": "implemented",
        "steps": [
          "Compute the time gap and the genre flag",
